# Web Testing Rules

Final QA is risk-based and follows PRD implementation.

## Priority Order

### 1. Visual Regression

- Exercise representative narrow, tablet, and desktop viewports
- Test dashboard loading, populated, empty, error, filtered, and detail states
- Use Playwright screenshots only where a visual regression is a meaningful risk
- If both themes exist, test both

### 2. Accessibility

- Run automated accessibility checks
- Test keyboard navigation
- Verify reduced-motion behavior
- Verify color contrast

### 3. Performance

- Run Lighthouse or equivalent against meaningful pages
- Keep CWV targets from [performance.mdc](performance.mdc)

### 4. Cross-Browser

- Select browser coverage from risk; at minimum verify the supported Chromium
  journey before expanding to Firefox and WebKit
- Test grid, charts, Worker integration, scrolling, and fallback behavior

### 5. Responsive

- Test 320, 375, 768, 1024, 1440, 1920
- Verify no overflow
- Verify touch interactions

## E2E Shape

```ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('dashboard supports the critical exploration journey', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/');
  await expect(page.locator('h1')).toBeVisible();
});
```

- Avoid flaky timeout-based assertions
- Prefer deterministic waits

## Unit Tests

- Test utilities, data transforms, and custom hooks
- For highly visual components, visual regression often carries more signal than brittle markup assertions
- Jest plus React Testing Library covers selected component and integration
  seams. No arbitrary coverage target applies.
